        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current changeover steps and pick the pilot line scope.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 10272,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the 'Standardise Assembly Line Changeover and Ergonomic Routines' project. First step is T1: mapping what we all do now. Can everyone share how they handle a changeover on their line? I'm thinking about the small things too, not just the big steps. What works, what doesn't?",
            "mentions": [
              81330,
              87884,
              375944
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 81330,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "On Line 2, I usually just clear the parts bins, wipe down the surface, and grab the new parts. The tool cart is sometimes messy so finding the right wrench can take a minute.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 375944,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Same for me. I just do what the person before me did.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 10272,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Thanks. That 'messy tool cart' is a good example of a bottleneck. Do you follow a specific order for safety checks, like checking guards or e-stops?",
            "mentions": [
              81330
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 81330,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Not really a formal check, I just make sure it looks ok before I start.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 87884,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Sorry for the delay. On Line 4, the process is different if we're switching to the larger engine blocks because we have to get the hoist. That adds time. Maybe we should pilot this on Line 4 since it has the most variation?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 10272,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "That's a great point, the variation on Line 4 would give us a good test. Let's propose that for the pilot. Does anyone object to using Line 4, maybe on the second shift to start?",
            "mentions": [
              81330,
              87884,
              375944
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 81330,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Line 4 second shift is fine with me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 10272,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Ok, decision made. We'll use Line 4, second shift, as the pilot. Now for the mapping in T1. It sounds like the current process is informal. We need to be specific.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 10272,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "I suggest we list every single action, from walking to the parts bin to the final safety check. We should also note down the time it takes for each, even if it's just an estimate. And let's make sure to capture those 'unsafe shortcuts' the project brief mentions. We can track this in the feedback log A8.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 87884,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "That level of detail sounds good. It will help us see where the delays are. I agree.",
            "mentions": [],
