      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Clarify time coding, payroll impact, and weekly reporting.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 371640,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I'm looking at T7 and need to clarify how we'll record time for these new routines. How much time are we expecting the changeover and the new ergonomic checks to take? This needs to be defined for the payroll rules in A7.",
            "mentions": [
              10272,
              81330,
              87884,
              375944
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7",
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 10272,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Good question. The ergonomic check should be quick, under 5 minutes at the start of the shift. The changeover time is what we're trying to reduce, but the pilot will give us a better number. Initially, it might be around 15-20 minutes.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 81330,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Does this count as standard time or will it be a special code?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 371640,
            "reply_to": "M50",
            "text": "That's the key question. Since it's part of the standard work but not direct production, the correct way to code the changeover time is 'Indirect Labor - Setup'. The ergonomic check and station rotation are part of the normal shift activities and don't need a separate code. They are just 'Regular Time'.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 87884,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "That makes sense. As long as it's all accounted for.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 371640,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "Exactly. So, can we agree on these rules for A7? Changeover time = 'Indirect Labor - Setup'. All other new activities = 'Regular Time'.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 10272,
            "reply_to": "M53",
            "text": "Yes, that's clear and logical. Agreed.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M55",
            "speaker_id": 371640,
            "reply_to": "M54",
            "text": "Great. Now for T8, the weekly performance summary. I've created a template, A6. It tracks average changeover time and the number of incidents from the log. The supervisor will be responsible for filling it out each Friday. Please take a look.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M56",
            "speaker_id": 87884,
            "reply_to": "M55",
            "text": "The template looks good for tracking data. Could we add a small section for 'Notes/Wins'? It would be good to capture positive feedback too, not just problems.",
